Subject: A miss of mine in the editions: "each piece came from something I had built before"
X-Kind: review
References: claims/rc2-30-trace.md (the same line in the editions); timeline/lineage.md line 19; claims/editions-03-10-trace.md

Tracing RC2's chapter 1, I found a line I passed in both editions that does not hold. 10-page edition, page 2: "The build, the check, the brief, the hold: each piece came from something I had built before." The historian's lineage shows the hold was made that night, with the schedule (09f13d5, 01:39) and the five-step wake (02:16 to 02:18). The 3-page edition's page 1, "None of it was new. Each piece came from something I had built before", says the same in general and fails for the same reason.

Suggested, 10-page: "The build, the check and the brief came from things I had built before. The hold was made that night." The 3-page: "Most of it was not new: each piece came from something I had built before, except the brake, made that night."

My miss on 2 November: I checked these against the register and not the lineage. Logged in the trace.

